# File-Scoped Template Preview QA Rule

## When This Rule Applies

- Any edit to preview routing, demo HTML pages, preview chrome, Crafto demo mappings, or audit scripts/reports.

## Required Checks Before Finishing

- Run link audit: `py scripts/audit_preview_header_footer_links.py`
- Run hash-link audit: `py scripts/audit_crafto_hash_links.py`
- Run title audit: `py scripts/audit_preview_titles.py`
- Run visual logo placement audit: `py scripts/audit_preview_logo_placement.py`
- Refresh report: `scripts/audit_report.txt`
- Confirm no Crafto/ThemeZaa user-facing branding in edited preview/template pages.
- Confirm favicon and primary logo in live preview pages use Mateo business assets (`mateo-favicon.ico`, `mateo-logo_horizontal_transparent.png`) at non-overlapping display size (`mkt-mateo-brand-logo`, desktop max 56px x 220px / mobile max 34px x 170px).
- Confirm header and footer text in wrapped previews do not contain "Crafto" or "ThemeZaa".
- Confirm wrapped preview `<title>` equals `Mateo Consulting Team - The Multipurpose HTML5 Template`.
- Confirm wrapped previews do not emit `/crafto/#` or bare `#`; map those to `/preview/{slug}/home`.
- Confirm preview links map to `/preview/{slug}/{page}` or gracefully fallback to `/preview/{slug}/home`.
- Confirm preview chrome header includes Mateo logo before the `Home` tab on all live preview pages.
- Confirm `artifacts/live-preview-audit/report.json` shows zero failures and review generated screenshots for visual overlap.
- Confirm edited pages have no missing CSS/JS/component references.

## Route + Fallback Standard

- Do not return broken preview-site paths.
- If an inner page is missing/unmapped, route to template home preview.
- Keep header/footer/navigation links consistent across the mapped page set.
